0..74 Comment "// Transport, the HoTT book\'s § 2.3 (`Path.walk`), along reflexivity at a"
75..150 Comment "// motive whose fibres are path types: the element it returns is a path, an"
151..226 Comment "// element of another type is none, and transport along the path it returns"
227..296 Comment "// runs it first. Along reflexivity, at a path-type motive and in the"
297..364 Comment "// universe, transport keeps the value, by conversion and by a run."
365..367 Comment "//"
368..403 Comment "// - see: #649 — `along_returned`"
